==Swedish==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|sv|gmq-osw|dygn}}, {{m|gmq-osw|dyghn}}, {{m|gmq-osw|døgn}}, {{m|gmq-osw|døghn}}, from {{inh|sv|non|dœgn}}, from {{inh|sv|gem-pro|*dōgin-}}, alternative form of {{m|gem-pro|*dōg-}}. {{etydate|mid-14th century|ref={{R:svenska.se|SO}}}}.

{{glossary|Cognate}} with {{cog|da|døgn}}, {{cog|nb|døgn}} and {{cog|nn|døgn}}. See also {{cog|non|dœgr}}, {{cog|nn|døger}} and {{cog|is|dægur}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|sv|/dʏŋn/}}
* {{audio|sv|LL-Q9027 (swe)-Moonhouse-dygn.wav}}

===Noun===
{{sv-noun|n}}

# [[day]], [[nychthemeron]] (24 hours)
#: {{ux|sv|hyran är 500 kronor per '''dygn'''|the rent is 500 SEK per '''24 hour'''}}
#: {{ux|sv|de var utan ström i nästan '''2 dygn'''|they were without electricity for almost '''48 hours'''}}
#: {{ux|sv|operationen fördröjdes '''3 dygn''' på grund av platsbrist|the surgery was postponed for '''72 hours''' due to lack of space}}
# [[day]] (specifically, the 24 hour period from midnight to the following midnight)
#:{{ux|sv|oavsett tid på '''dygnet'''|any time of '''day'''|lit=regardless time of '''day'''}}
#:{{ux|sv|öppet '''dygnet''' runt|open '''24 hours'''|lit=open '''the day''' around}}
#:{{ux|sv|vägen stängdes i 5 '''dygn''' på grund av rasmassorna|the road closed for 5 '''days''' due to the debris}}

====Usage notes====
* The difference between {{m|sv|dag||day}} and {{m-self|sv|dygn||day}}. Imagine it is around 3 o'clock on a Monday; if someone says:
** ''"Om 4 '''dagar''' är jag på stranden"'' ("In 4 days I am on the beach"), meaning that they will be on the beach on Friday.
** ''"Om 4 '''dygn''' är jag på stranden"'' ("In 4 days I am on the beach"), meaning that they will be on the beach around 3 o'clock on Friday.

